  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "Split Button",
    "Description",
    "Primary action + chevron trigger that opens a menu of related secondary actions. Use when one action dominates but alternatives are sometimes needed (Save / Save as / Save and close). For 3+ equal-weight actions use Button Group; for a pure menu trigger use Dropdown. The two halves share the same prio and size.",
    "Priority & Size",
    "prio=primary       Filled. One per screen region at most.\nprio=secondary   Outlined. Use in toolbars and detail headers.\n\nsize=sm (36px)    Toolbars, inspector headers.\nsize=md (44px)    Default for page-level actions.",
    "Composition",
    "Left half: the dominant action. Click fires it directly, no menu.\nRight half (chevron): opens a menu listing 2–5 alternative actions.\n\nThe alternatives must be *variants* of the dominant action, not unrelated. If the menu actions diverge (Save + Delete + Archive), use a Dropdown or a Context Menu instead.",
    "Accessibility",
    "Two <button>s in a joined container. The chevron button exposes aria-haspopup=\"menu\" and aria-expanded. Menu items are role=\"menuitem\". Keyboard: Tab into primary; Alt+Down opens menu from primary; ↓/↑ navigate menu; Esc closes. Focus ring wraps whichever half is focused, not the whole control.",
    "Rules",
    "Do\n\n• Keep the menu actions as variants of the primary\n• Share prio and size between the two halves\n• Use aria-haspopup + aria-expanded on the chevron\n• Close the menu on Esc",
    "Don't\n\n• Don't put unrelated actions in the menu — use Dropdown\n• Don't use for 3+ equal-weight actions — use Button Group\n• Don't use different prio on the two halves\n• Don't auto-open the menu on hover"
  ],
  "pageContext": null
}
